    "available_at": "2026-11-17T10:21:04.526978+00:00",
    "body": "PARIS — French troops have been operating in Ukraine in non-combat roles since at least the summer of 2026 to maintain equipment used by the Ukrainian armed forces and provide training, Radio France Internationale reported, citing several unidentified sources familiar with the deployment.\nThe troops are part of a structure called Volia, after a Ukrainian word that can be translated as “will” or “freedom,” the French state-owned international news radio said on Monday . Volia is headed by a French general, and French troops operating in Ukraine are deployed under the guise of the Gerfaut mission in Poland to train Ukrainian soldiers, RFI said.\nFrance has supplied Ukraine with equipment including Caesar howitzers, Mirage 2000 jets and precision missiles, for which maintenance expertise is being provided by personnel from various French support regiments, according to RFI. The radio broadcaster said it’s not disclosing the names of regiments involved to ensure the safety of soldiers and those around them.\nThe United Kingdom has also reportedly deployed troops in Ukraine in non-combat roles. Two serving members of the British armed forces are known to have died in the country since Russia’s 2022 invasion, with the U.K. Ministry of Defence confirming both deaths as non-combat accidents away from the front lines.\nThe structure of Volia is “light and modular,” composed of small teams for short-term missions, and Volia is not a combat mission, according to RFI. France decided against sending civilian technicians because Ukraine is at war, the radio broadcaster said.\nWhile France’s constitution requires the government inform parliament of a conventional force deployment outside the national territory, neither the National Assembly nor the Senate have been informed of the existence of Volia, RFI reported.\nMeanwhile, TV broadcaster France Télévisions similarly reported on Monday that France has secretly deployed several dozens of military in Ukraine as part of Volia. The outlet said it had confirmed the RFI information, but it did not disclose how.",
